I do remember.
我确实记得。

00:25:18.269 --> 00:25:19.150
I mean, you just been in the neighborhood.
我是说，你刚好就在附近。

00:25:19.150 --> 00:25:19.990
He was just around.
他就在周围。

00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:21.670
I think he was just around.
我觉得他只是正好在附近。

00:25:21.670 --> 00:25:25.789
But I remember, I was like, I had the yips.
但我记得，当时我有点怯场。

00:25:25.789 --> 00:25:28.750
Like, I was like, how do you talk to Victoria's Secret models?
就像是，我心想：你该怎么跟维多利亚的秘密模特说话？

00:25:28.750 --> 00:25:29.910
Like, I didn't know.
我根本不知道。

00:25:29.910 --> 00:25:31.349
Suddenly there were eight of them.
突然之间周围出现了八个。

00:25:31.349 --> 00:25:42.390
And I was just like, I just remember, I talked to, I talked to Adriana Lima about ayahuasca because I had just gotten back from Brazil, and that was my only line.
我只记得，我跟阿德里亚娜·利马（Adriana Lima）聊了死藤水（ayahuasca），因为我刚从巴西回来，那是我唯一的聊天切入点。

00:25:42.390 --> 00:26:06.869
That was all I had and she was very nice, but it was just like the only way I can describe it when I said before, it felt like we were guest stars on our own show because the collective power of the Victoria's Secret models at that time were dwarfed, like were series regulars on a CBS show, like, they were, they had a buzz in the air about them and they had made this huge set.
我就这点存货了，她人非常好，但那种感觉就像我之前说的，感觉我们像是自己剧集里的客串演员，因为当时维密模特们的集体气场太强大了，就像是CBS节目的常驻演员一样，她们自带一种光环，而且剧组还搭建了这么大一个场景。

00:26:06.869 --> 00:26:13.950
It felt like we didn't know, and there were so many extras around, like, I just remember feeling like an aerial view.
感觉我们整个人都是懵的，周围有那么多的群演，我只记得那种感觉就像是在上帝视角。

00:26:13.950 --> 00:26:19.190
I felt like Neil and I were just pinballing from like little vignette to little vignette.
我觉得我和尼尔就像是在不同的场景之间像弹球一样到处乱撞。

00:26:19.190 --> 00:26:24.230
We were lost in this huge set full of Victoria's secret models and we did not know what to do.
我们在满是维密模特的巨大片场里迷失了方向，完全不知道该怎么办。

00:26:24.230 --> 00:26:25.230
We did not know what to do.
完全不知道该怎么办。

00:26:25.230 --> 00:26:29.670
We were lost children in a strange land and we didn't quite know what to do and the whole.
我们就像是误入异乡的迷失儿童，完全不知所措，整个。

00:26:29.670 --> 00:26:39.289
And I also think that, you know, we're going to get to this episode, but are probably our most famous, like, stunt cast, although I don't even know if that's the right term.
而且我也觉得，咱们等下会聊到这一集，但这可能是我们最著名的大牌客串——虽然我甚至不知道这词准不准。

00:26:39.289 --> 00:26:48.109
But like, the way you guys used, uh, Britney Spears, yeah, and also what I thought was so brilliant about this.
但你们用布兰妮·斯皮尔斯的这种方式，对，而且我也觉得这一集最妙的地方在于。

00:26:48.109 --> 00:26:49.190
And again, we'll talk about this.
再次重申，我们待会儿会聊到这个。

00:26:49.190 --> 00:26:50.190
You did not.
你们没有。

00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:51.670
You flipped the story for her.
你们为她反转了人设。

00:26:51.670 --> 00:26:53.109
We didn't create the story for her.
我们并没有为她量身打造这个故事。

00:26:53.109 --> 00:26:54.109
She heard her folks.
是她那边主动找来的。

00:26:54.109 --> 00:26:55.910
That was an incoming call.
那是主动找上门的合作。

00:26:55.910 --> 00:26:59.630
Her folks were like, we, we want her to do this and we're like, here's what we got.
她团队的人说，我们，我们想让她演这个，然后我们就说，那我们手里有这些。

00:26:59.630 --> 00:27:11.150
But what was so sweet about it was, this is someone who everyone knows has spent her whole life as the object of, you know, prurient interest and sexual fascination and all these kinds of things.
但最妙的是，大家都知道这个人一辈子都生活在各种低俗趣味、性吸引力以及诸如此类的目光焦点下。

00:27:11.150 --> 00:27:17.933
But you made her this kind of sweet, sweet-maptious wallflower who was in love, hopelessly with Ted.
但你们把她塑造得像个可爱、单纯、有点社恐的壁花小姐，无可救药地爱着泰德。

00:27:17.933 --> 00:27:34.349
I don't know it allowed something very sweet and honest, and she was like very endearing in the part, but it didn't highlight, I think the Victoria Secret models were playing Victoria's Secret models, so there was nothing subversive about it.
我不知道，这让剧情变得非常甜美和真诚，她在剧中的表现也非常讨人喜欢，但并没有刻意放大——我觉得维秘模特们当时就是在演维秘模特，所以并没有什么颠覆性。

00:27:34.910 --> 00:27:38.778
Yeah, yeah, I think ultimately we didn't quite know what to do with it.
对，对，我觉得最终我们其实也不知道该怎么处理。

00:27:38.778 --> 00:27:48.478
We were given this thing, we were given this prompt, sometimes you're given a prompt like the two severed heads and you're like, I'm gonna come up with something crazy with this.
我们接到了这个任务，接到了这个命题，有时你接到的命题就像那两个断头，你会觉得：我要用这个搞点疯狂的点子出来。

00:27:48.478 --> 00:27:51.802
And this one was like, it was a hard puzzle to solve somehow.
而这一集就像是，某种很难解开的谜题。

00:27:51.802 --> 00:28:01.230
And I think if we could do it over again, I thought, giving a more emotional co-story alongside this Barney Victoria secret models thing that we were told you're doing this.
我想如果能重来一次，我觉得，除了巴尼和维密模特这条线之外——当时公司告诉我们必须得这么拍，说会有巴尼，会有维密模特，而且我们要宣传它。

00:28:01.230 --> 00:28:04.430
It's gonna be Barney, it's gonna be Victoria secret models and we're gonna promote it.
这集里会有巴尼，会有维密模特，我们要宣传。

00:28:04.430 --> 00:28:08.670
We're gonna shoot promos with the Victoria secret models for the show like original promos.
我们要和维密模特为这部剧拍摄宣传片，原创宣传片那种。

00:28:08.670 --> 00:28:14.950
Remember we did that, we probably had to write them or rewrite them, we were often handed these promos that were like, not quite right.
还记得我们拍过那个吗？我们可能还得自己写或者改剧本，我们经常会拿到那种不太合适的宣传片。

00:28:14.950 --> 00:28:19.069
And we'd have to like spend part of our week rewriting the promos and then shooting them like this.
然后我们得花一部分时间来重写宣传片，然后再像这样把它们拍出来。

00:28:19.069 --> 00:28:21.990
Yeah, we did that a lot, but it's part of the job.
对，我们以前经常这样，但这也是工作的一部分。

00:28:21.990 --> 00:28:25.589
It's part of, there is this commerce aspect to it.
这就是，这里面确实有商业考量。

00:28:25.589 --> 00:28:35.069
And you're like, we need to stay a hit show, we need to get a lot of viewers, and that will enable us to keep being artists in other later episodes that aren't this one.
你会想：我们需要保持收视长虹，我们需要吸引大量观众，这才能让我们在接下来的其他非这一集的剧集里继续当艺术家。

00:28:35.069 --> 00:28:37.269
And this one feels that way a little.
而这一集确实有点那种味道。

00:28:37.269 --> 00:28:43.069
And then you're reminded that the show is interrupted every seven or eight minutes for Chevy ads or whatever.
然后你就会被提醒，这部剧每隔七八分钟就会插播雪佛兰的广告什么的。

00:28:43.069 --> 00:28:43.910
Absolutely.
绝对是这样。

00:28:43.910 --> 00:28:47.470
For ads for stay tuned for the Victoria's Secret Special.
插播着“请锁定收看维多利亚的秘密特别节目”的广告。

00:28:47.470 --> 00:28:50.710
Yeah, you know, it's just this was some corporate synergy.
对，你知道的，这就是所谓的企业协同效应。

00:28:50.710 --> 00:28:52.910
We got corporate synergy a little bit on this one.
我们在这一集里确实体验了一把企业协同效应。

00:28:52.910 --> 00:28:53.950
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:28:53.950 --> 00:28:55.549
There was a bunch of good stuff in this episode.
这一集里有很多精彩的内容。

00:28:55.549 --> 00:29:00.309
Stephanie Farracy, as I hope I'm saying her name right, as Rhonda, who- Fantastic.
斯蒂法尼·法拉西（Stephanie Faracy），希望我没念错她的名字，饰演朗达，她——太棒了。

00:29:00.309 --> 00:29:01.750
Virginity was great.
关于保持处女之身的设定太棒了。

00:29:01.750 --> 00:29:06.430
She was a last minute break glass in case of emergency piece of casting.
她是最后关头“紧急情况砸碎玻璃”备用的选角。

00:29:06.430 --> 00:29:07.349
We cast somebody else.
我们本来选了另一个人。

00:29:07.349 --> 00:29:08.910
I remember this very well.
这事我记得非常清楚。

00:29:08.910 --> 00:29:11.230
Not to work out in a bit of a weird way.
结果过程有点诡异，不太顺利。

00:29:11.230 --> 00:29:12.269
This is a weird week.
那是个奇怪的一周。

00:29:12.269 --> 00:29:16.630
I didn't have any scenes with this person who shall remain nameless.
我和这位恕我直言不讳的演员没有对手戏。

00:29:16.630 --> 00:29:18.069
Yes.
对。

00:29:18.069 --> 00:29:21.710
But I didn't have any scenes with this person, but I remember we rehearsed with her, right?
虽然我和这个人没有对手戏，但我记得我们跟她一起排练过，对吧？

00:29:21.710 --> 00:29:24.630
She wasn't doing great, I think, emotionally.
我觉得她当时状态不太好，情绪上有点问题。

00:29:24.630 --> 00:29:37.109
I think there was some stuff going on, and we had to part ways at the last minute and bring in Stephanie who came in like, she did not have the yips, she knew the assignment.
好像有些状况发生，我们不得不在最后一刻分道扬镳，换成了斯蒂法尼。她来的时候——她可没有怯场，她完全懂她的任务。

00:29:37.109 --> 00:29:39.990
She came in off the bench and fucking nailed it.
她临危受命，表现得太神了。

00:29:39.990 --> 00:29:43.789
She was great, we probably hired her the night before we started shooting.
她表现得太棒了，我们大概是在开拍前一天晚上才雇她的。

00:29:43.789 --> 00:29:46.990
I wanna say, maybe we hired her for the run-through.
我想说，也许我们是排练时才雇她的。

00:29:46.990 --> 00:29:51.470
It only happened about two or three times in the history of how our mother wears.
在《老爸老妈浪漫史》的历史上，这种情况大概也就发生过两三次。

00:29:51.470 --> 00:29:52.829
The history, we can't name any names.
历史上，我们不能点名道姓。

00:29:52.829 --> 00:29:57.470
You rehearse Monday and Tuesday with someone and you show up to shoot Wednesday and you're like, oh hello.
你周一和周二跟某个人排练，结果周三去片场时你会想：哦，你好啊。

00:29:57.470 --> 00:29:59.230
You're not the person we've been working with.
你不是我们之前一起合作的那个人。

00:29:59.230 --> 00:30:00.950
Belly full of Turkey had happened.
吃了一肚子火鸡肉这种事也发生过。

00:30:00.950 --> 00:30:08.430
Marshall's dad was gonna be a different actor and it, again, something weird did not work out and we can't talk about it.
马修的爸爸原本打算由另一位演员出演，但同样地，出了点奇怪的状况没谈拢，具体是谁我们不能说。

00:30:08.430 --> 00:30:39.180
I remember it happened another time with a woman who, This was actually, this is kind of a sweet story, but we rehearsed, I think it was, I can't remember we've even seen this episode yet, but there was a really sweet, wonderful actress who was rehearsing with us Monday and Tuesday and then they fired her and they bumped up the, I think it was in Ted Mosby architect actually.
我记得还有一次，有个女演员——这其实是个挺暖心的故事，我们排练过，我想是，我不记得我们当时拍没拍到那一集，但有个非常甜美、优秀的男（女）演员周一和周二跟我们一起排练，结果他们把她给开除了，换上了——我记得那集其实是《泰德·莫斯比，建筑师》。

00:30:39.180 --> 00:30:40.500
Have we already done that episode?
那一集我们已经聊过了吗？

00:30:40.500 --> 00:30:41.339
We did.
聊过了。

00:30:41.339 --> 00:30:42.460
Did we talk about this?
我们聊过这个吗？

00:30:42.460 --> 00:30:51.579
I mean, yeah, I don't think they replaced this actress, but I had been fired, remember, on Off Center, that first pilot I did, right?
我是说，对，我觉得他们并没有替换这个女演员，不过我记得我以前在拍《中产阶级》（Off Center）——我拍的第一个试播集时也被炒过，对吧？

00:30:51.579 --> 00:31:01.259
And I asked casting if I could have her email, and I wrote her and I told her the story about, because I figured she's probably horrified, you know?
我问选角导演能不能把她的邮箱给我，我给她写了信，把我在《中产阶级》被开除的故事告诉了她，因为我想她当时肯定吓坏了吧？

00:31:01.259 --> 00:31:04.619
She got replaced, and she was good, too.
她被换掉了，而且她演得很好。

00:31:04.619 --> 00:31:06.299
She was really good.
她真的很棒。

00:31:06.299 --> 00:31:07.700
I forget this, you'll have to tell me how it happened.
我都忘了这事了，你得跟我讲讲当时是怎么回事。

00:31:07.700 --> 00:31:15.140
And I wrote her an email, and I told her the story about my getting cast, I mean, getting fired on off center.
我给她写了一封邮件，把我在《中产阶级》被开除的经历讲给她听。

00:31:15.140 --> 00:31:19.579
And, you know, she obviously knew now that I was starring on how I met your mother.
而且，你知道的，她当时显然已经知道我是《老爸老妈浪漫史》的主演了。

00:31:19.579 --> 00:31:22.500
And then she ended up on a really big show.
后来她去了一部非常大火的剧。

00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:23.819
She's had a good career.
她的职业生涯发展得很顺利。

00:31:23.819 --> 00:31:25.980
She's like done really well.
她现在混得相当不错。

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:31.430
And I ran into her, I think I ran into her with Jordana.
后来我偶遇过她，我想我跟乔丹娜（Jordana）一起遇到过她。

00:31:31.430 --> 00:31:32.549
I think I did.
我想是的。

00:31:32.549 --> 00:31:37.390
And she said, you wrote me the sweetest email.
她说，你给我写过最甜蜜的电子邮件。

00:31:37.390 --> 00:31:39.950
And for a minute, I was like, I forgot what the email was.
有一会儿，我心想，我都忘了那封邮件写的是什么了。

00:31:39.950 --> 00:31:43.269
And I was like, oh my God, I'm in front of my wife, what did I write in his email?
然后我想，天哪，我当着我老婆的面呢，我在他这封邮件里都写了些什么？

00:31:43.269 --> 00:31:48.990
But she said, you just told me about getting fired and I never forgot it and it was so- So I am about to be recast in my marriage.
但她说，你只是跟我聊了聊被解雇的事，我一直没忘，而且太——所以我差点在婚姻里被换角。

00:31:48.990 --> 00:31:50.549
Yes.
对。

00:31:50.549 --> 00:31:57.029
But it's great for anyone who has a career knock or gets fired or that.
但这对于任何遭遇职业打击、被解雇或类似情况的人来说都是件好事。

00:31:57.029 --> 00:31:57.869
It's really nice to do that.
这样做真的很好。

00:31:57.869 --> 00:32:00.190
It gives you a super power to help other people.
它会赋予你一种超级力量去帮助其他人。

00:32:00.190 --> 00:32:01.029
Yes, yes, yes.
对，对，对。

00:32:01.029 --> 00:32:04.349
Because you know you land on your feet or you know, so I was able to help this person.
因为你知道你会东山再起，或者你知道的，所以我得以帮助这个人。

00:32:04.349 --> 00:32:08.869
But all of which is to say, show business is brutal and sometimes people get replaced.
但总而言之，演艺圈是残酷的，有时人们会被替代。

00:32:08.869 --> 00:32:18.710
And this old man, he mustered me, fell in love with you, new York City.
而这个老头，他鼓起勇气，爱上了你，纽约市。

00:32:18.710 --> 00:32:28.250
And now, commercials.
现在是广告时间。

00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:33.190
End of commercials, back to show.
广告结束，回到节目。

00:32:33.190 --> 00:32:39.589
So this was a really weird production week when I remember that story too, which I did not remember when we started talking about this episode.
所以当我回想起那个故事时，这也是一个非常奇怪的制作周，当我们开始聊这一集时，我本来已经不记得了。

00:32:39.589 --> 00:32:43.230
I'm glad you remembered that because you're talking about Victoria's Secret models.
很高兴你还记得，因为你在谈论维多利亚的秘密模特。

00:32:43.230 --> 00:32:54.769
There's another fairly well-known actress who gets, we let them go and we bring in someone else last minute to play a really important role, like the biggest part of the story is Barney and this woman Rhonda.
还有另一位相当知名的女演员，我们让她走，然后在最后一分钟带来另一个人来扮演一个非常重要的角色，就像故事中最重大的部分是巴尼和这个叫龙达的女人。

00:32:54.769 --> 00:33:05.309
And this was just a spooky, weird, you know, spit and duct tape holding it together a week on the How I Met Your Mother stuff, but we somehow got it done.
这只是《老爸老妈浪漫史》剧组中令人毛骨悚然、奇怪的一周，全靠唾沫和电工胶带勉强维持，但我们不知怎么地还是完成了。

00:33:05.309 --> 00:33:06.470
There's a bunch of good stuff.
有很多不错的内容。

00:33:06.470 --> 00:33:08.789
It's not an all-timer, but it holds it together.
它虽然不是史上最佳，但整体还算撑得过去。

00:33:08.789 --> 00:33:12.710
And we got some nice promos on the back of the show.
而且我们在节目后半段获得了一些不错的宣传片。

00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:23.819
The big reveal for me of this episode, the thing I take away that I say, all right, this This is why this episode had to happen, is we learn that Barney slept with Madeleine Albright.
对我来说，这一集最大的揭秘，我从中领悟到并觉得“好吧，这就是这一集必须发生的原因”，是我们得知巴尼和马德琳·奥尔布赖特睡过。

00:33:23.819 --> 00:33:30.579
I mean, it's I mean, unfortunately, that's the episode you want to see, why are we watching this one?
我的意思是，这——不幸的是，那是你想看的剧集，为什么我们要看这一集？

00:33:30.579 --> 00:33:31.579
I don't want to see Victoria's secret models.
我不想看维多利亚的秘密模特。

00:33:31.579 --> 00:33:34.500
I want to see Barney and Madeleine Albright getting it done.
我想看巴尼和马德琳·奥尔布赖特成其好事。

00:33:34.500 --> 00:33:39.779
Was this also, this might have been the debut of Ted's Wesleyan shirt when he's working out?
这也是——这可能是泰德在锻炼时穿的那件卫斯理大学T恤的首秀吗？

00:33:39.779 --> 00:33:41.460
Or are you born that before?
还是说你之前就穿过？

00:33:41.460 --> 00:33:42.619
No, he had to get rid of it before.
不，他之前必须把它扔掉。

00:33:42.619 --> 00:33:43.619
I still have it, by the way.
顺便说一句，我还留着它。

00:33:43.619 --> 00:33:44.619
I still have that.
我手里还留着呢。

00:33:44.619 --> 00:33:45.619
Well, you're an honorary.
好吧，你是个荣誉成员。

00:33:45.619 --> 00:33:46.619
You're a distinguished.
你是个杰出人士。

