米克锻炼得很刻苦。

00:34:11.067 --> 00:34:14.579
Like, Mick was like, Like Mick was like an Iron Man kind of guy.
就像，米克就像是——米克就像那种铁人三项类型的人。

00:34:14.579 --> 00:34:30.179
And because, so the stand-in as people may or may not know, when they light the scene and block the scene, well we've blocked it, you know, and the stand-ins watch us, the rehearsal, and then they recreate our blocking and they light the scenes and focus the cameras and do all that.
因为，替身正如人们可能知道或不知道的那样，当他们为场景打光和走位时，我们已经走过位了，你知道的，替身会看我们排练，然后他们重现我们的走位，为场景打光、调整摄像机焦点并做所有这些事。

00:34:30.179 --> 00:34:37.420
So we're away, we often get sent away and we come back and sometimes our stand-ins like tell us, okay there's been this little change, you're now going to stand here.
所以我们不在场，我们经常被支开，然后我们回来，有时我们的替身会告诉我们，好吧，这里有个小改动，你现在要站在这里。

00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:44.380
And you know if you do it for nine years and the stand-in crew is stable, which ours is what, you get to know these people really well.
你知道，如果你干了九年，替身团队很稳定，就像我们这样，你就会非常了解这些人。

00:34:44.380 --> 00:35:02.219
And they just, they help you, it's a really symbiotic relationship, but Mick was my standard for years, and I had this joke with him, which is actually funny that he was in this episode, because Mick would like do a nine mile run in the morning before he came to work, okay?
他们会帮你，这是一种真正的共生关系，但米克当了我多年的替身，我和他有个笑话，他能出现在这一集里其实挺搞笑的，因为米克在来上班的早上会进行九英里的长跑，好吧？

00:35:02.219 --> 00:35:03.659
This is why we cast him in this video.
这就是为什么我们让他在这段视频里出镜。

00:35:03.659 --> 00:35:12.000
And I would always say like, how long did you, but it became like, because he was my stand-in, I was getting the benefits of his workouts, Like that was our joke.
我总是会说，你跑了多久，但这就变成了——因为他是我的替身，我在享受他锻炼的成果，这就是我们的笑话。

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:14.500
So I could say like, how long did we run this morning?
所以我可以问，我们今天早上跑了多久？

00:35:14.500 --> 00:35:16.420
He's like, we did a good eight miles this morning.
他说，我们今天早上跑了整整八英里。

00:35:16.420 --> 00:35:17.539
I'm like, I feel it, man.
我说，我能感觉到，老兄。

00:35:17.539 --> 00:35:18.980
I feel good.
我感觉很好。

00:35:18.980 --> 00:35:25.820
So shout out to Mick and our workouts for many years that I was the beneficiary of his artwork.
所以要感谢米克以及我们多年的锻炼，我曾受益于他的成果。

00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:28.420
He must still be doing it, Josh, because you look great.
他肯定还在坚持，乔希，因为你看起来棒极了。

00:35:28.420 --> 00:35:29.420
Do I?
是吗？

00:35:29.420 --> 00:35:29.920
Yeah.
对。

00:35:29.920 --> 00:35:30.420
You look great.
你看起来状态很好。

00:35:30.420 --> 00:35:35.219
What if I start just losing it and I call Mick, I'm like, dude, what's going on?
如果我开始状态下滑，然后打电话给米克，说，老兄，怎么回事？

00:35:35.219 --> 00:35:37.019
Why are we looking like this?
为什么我们变成这样了？

00:35:37.019 --> 00:35:39.219
I'm like, yeah, that's really fine.
我说，好吧，那真的挺好。

00:35:39.219 --> 00:35:39.719
Yeah.
对。

00:35:39.719 --> 00:35:51.320
So shout out to Mick and, you know, I'm glad we had this episode, Craig, because I think when people, you know, people ask me like, was how I met your mother just so much fun all the time?
所以要感谢米克，而且，你知道，我很高兴我们录了这一期节目，克雷格，因为我觉得当人们，你知道，人们问我，难道《老爸老妈浪漫史》一直都那么有趣吗？

00:35:51.320 --> 00:36:00.800
Because they see the blooper reel, they think it's, and it's like, no, it was nine years of our lives, which means some days you show up at your best and some days you show up at your worst.
因为他们看到了搞笑花絮，就以为是这样，而事实上，那是我们生活中的九年，这意味着有些日子你展现出最好的状态，而有些日子你展现出最糟的状态。

00:36:00.800 --> 00:36:22.907
And a lot of days you just show up and it's still a job, it's still like a thing that you showed up for and you know it was more fun and it was really well-paying and it was you know there were a lot of things but it was still same with the writers like some days you nail it as a writer and some days you know you just got to get back to the back in front of the typewriter in the next day.
很多时候你只是去上班，它依然是一份工作，依然是你不得不去完成的一摊事，你知道它更有趣，报酬也很丰厚，你知道有很多方面，但它依然是工作，对编剧来说也一样，有些日子你作为编剧灵感爆发，而有些日子，你知道，第二天你只能重新坐回打字机前。

00:36:22.907 --> 00:36:32.180
Yeah this is like we were given something we had to do and sometimes that like really inspires you and other times it's like, I, how do we, how do we pull this off?
对，这就好像我们被赋予了必须完成的任务，有时那真的会激励你，而另一些时候你会想，我，我们该怎么，怎么搞定这个？

00:36:32.180 --> 00:36:34.668
And you, so I, I think we, we pulled it off.
所以你，我想我们，我们做到了。

00:36:34.668 --> 00:36:41.340
I think it's a, it's a, it had, there's some fun stuff, but it's not the greatest, it's not the greatest way to start.
我觉得它，它里面有一些很有趣的东西，但它并不是最棒的，这不是最好的开端。

00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:45.750
We didn't, we, we, we felt, we luxuriated in the blank page, the next episode.
我们没有，我们，我们，我们沉浸在空白的页面中，准备下一集。

00:36:45.750 --> 00:36:50.669
I guarantee you the next one up, we're like, okay, I'm glad there's no parameters here.
我向你保证，接下来那一集，我们会觉得，好吧，我很高兴这里没有任何限制。

00:36:50.669 --> 00:36:53.892
I want to say that our talk about this episode, the yips.
我想说我们对这一集的讨论，也就是“心魔”。

00:36:53.892 --> 00:36:55.079
Yeah, I have enjoyed.
对，我很享受。

