Just go to how we made your mother.com, H-W-M-Y-M, go to contact and follow the directions.
只需访问 how we made your mother.com，即 H-W-M-Y-M，点击联系方式并按照说明操作。

00:37:53.039 --> 00:37:56.559
All right, so we've got a great letter today from Josh.
好的，我们今天收到了一封来自乔希的精彩信件。

00:37:56.559 --> 00:37:58.360
No relation.
同名同姓而已。

00:37:58.360 --> 00:38:00.199
Hi, Craig Josh and Alec.
嗨，克雷格、乔希和亚历克。

00:38:00.199 --> 00:38:03.639
I was a soldier in Iraq in 2007.
我曾在2007年作为一名士兵在伊拉克服役。

00:38:03.639 --> 00:38:05.800
One of the guys in my platoon had the first season of him.
我排里的一个人收到了寄给他的《老爸老妈浪漫史》第一季。

00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:07.199
You mailed to him.
你寄给他的。

00:38:07.199 --> 00:38:11.000
All the guys in third squad would gather around and watch the episodes together.
第三班的所有人都会聚在一起，一起看剧。

00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:13.440
They could get loud and rambunctious as they watched.
他们在观看时可能会又吵闹又喧哗。

00:38:13.440 --> 00:38:19.960
I saw a minute here and there, but I stood behind them and watched my whole first episode, the best prom ever.
我零星看过几分钟，但我站在他们身后看完了我的第一整集，即“最棒的舞会”。

00:38:19.960 --> 00:38:20.760
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

00:38:20.760 --> 00:38:23.079
I loved Barney trying to get into the dance.
我喜欢巴尼试图混进舞会。

00:38:23.079 --> 00:38:26.000
I remember after telling my buddy, what's the point of this show?
我记得看完后我对好友说，这剧有什么意义？

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:28.320
It's obvious Robin is the mom.
罗宾很显然就是老妈嘛。

00:38:28.320 --> 00:38:41.480
I didn't watch any more episodes that deployment, but the night we came back from Iraq, which was in March, 2008, after we went to dinner and had way too many drinks, I was able to get a designated driver to take me to Best Buy, and I bought season one and two on DVD.
那次部署期间我没有再看其他集，但在我们从伊拉克回来的那天晚上，也就是2008年3月，在去吃晚饭并喝了太多酒之后，我找了一个代驾带我去百思买，我在那儿买了一、二季的DVD。

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:43.320
This is the best drunk purchase I've ever heard of.
这是我听过最棒的酒后购物经历。

00:38:43.320 --> 00:38:44.840
That's how it should be bought.
这才是买剧的正确打开方式。

00:38:44.840 --> 00:38:48.760
Our barracks were three soldiers to a room, and each building was for a single platoon.
我们的营房是一个房间住三名士兵，每栋楼供一个排使用。

00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:51.239
I was lucky enough to have two of my best friends living with me.
我很幸运，有两位最好的朋友和我住在一起。

00:38:51.239 --> 00:38:52.880
We all sat down and watched him and him together.
我们都坐下来，一起看他和他们。

00:38:52.880 --> 00:38:58.079
What a surprise when I saw the pilot, and Ted told his kids that was how he met there and Robin.
当我看到试播集，泰德告诉他的孩子们那就是他和罗宾相遇的经过时，我感到多么惊讶。

00:38:58.079 --> 00:39:05.639
We always left our doors open and people would wander in and out and some would sit and watch an episode or tell us how great it was that it's seen it on our deployment.
我们总是把门开着，人们会进进出出，有些人会坐下来看上一集，或者告诉我们在我们执行任务时看到这个节目有多棒。

00:39:05.639 --> 00:39:12.320
By the time season three came out, both of my roommates had moved off post but still maintained a barracks room since they were paying their rent out of their own pocket.
到了第三季出来的时候，我的两个室友都已经搬离了驻地，但由于他们自掏腰包付房租，所以仍然保留着一个兵营宿舍。

00:39:12.320 --> 00:39:15.800
They would still come and hang out with me and we watched season three together.
他们还是会来找我玩，我们一起看了第三季。

00:39:15.800 --> 00:39:21.599
One of my roommates and I got out of the army together and moved to Washington and we were finally able to watch season four live on TV.
我和其中一个室友一起退伍，搬到了华盛顿，我们终于能在电视上看到第四季的直播了。

00:39:21.599 --> 00:39:24.119
the only season I've seen broadcast live.
这也是我看过的唯一一季电视直播。

00:39:24.119 --> 00:39:27.400
In 2015, I was married and out of college.
2015年，我结婚了，也大学毕业了。

00:39:27.400 --> 00:39:32.599
I was able to convince my wife and sister-in-law, who was living with us at the time, to watch him from start to finish.
我成功说服了我的妻子和当时和我们住在一起的小姨子，从头到尾一起看这部剧。

00:39:32.599 --> 00:39:34.440
I hadn't seen season nine yet.
我当时还没看过第九季。

00:39:34.440 --> 00:39:37.760
I told my wife I was wanting to see the end with her.
我告诉妻子，我想和她一起看大结局。

00:39:37.760 --> 00:39:47.239
My wife and sister-in-law speak Spanish and don't like watching things subtitled and prefer to watch it dubbed, but the DVDs don't have dubbed audio tracks.
我妻子和小姨子说西班牙语，不喜欢看有字幕的内容，更喜欢看配音版，但DVD没有配音音轨。

00:39:47.239 --> 00:39:48.079
Why?
为什么？

00:39:48.079 --> 00:39:51.239
When the show is dubbed and is played over air in Spanish.
当这部剧被配音并在西班牙语地区播出时。

00:39:51.239 --> 00:40:00.039
I asked them to watch just the first four episodes to decide whether they would want to watch an entire nine seasons in English, and they loved the show, and we watched the entire series together.
我请求她们只看前四集，然后决定是否想用英语看完整整九季，结果她们非常喜欢这部剧，我们一起看完了整个系列。

00:40:00.039 --> 00:40:09.159
It was nice to share something that I love for such a long time with my wife, and watching it with my sister-in-law is when we became friends, and she stopped being just my wife's sister.
能和妻子分享我长久以来喜爱的事物感觉真好，而和我的小姨子一起看剧，则让我们成为了朋友，她不再仅仅是我妻子的妹妹。

00:40:09.159 --> 00:40:13.599
I want to give a shout-out to the team that added the Spanish subtitles.
我想向添加西班牙语字幕的团队表示感谢。

00:40:13.599 --> 00:40:24.440
Spanish is my second language, but I think they did the best job out of anything I've seen their work translating the songs on the show still rhymes makes sense is still funny.
西班牙语是我的第二语言，但我认为他们做出了我见过的最好的工作，他们对剧中歌曲的翻译依然押辙、通顺且有趣。

00:40:24.440 --> 00:40:25.419
This is great.
这太棒了。

00:40:25.419 --> 00:40:31.853
They went with the spirit of the song and not a direct literal translation and it's awesome.
他们遵循了歌曲的精神，而不是生硬的直译，这太赞了。

00:40:31.853 --> 00:40:34.371
Thanks for the show and the podcast.
感谢这部剧和这个播客。

00:40:34.371 --> 00:40:34.871
Wow.
哇。

00:40:34.871 --> 00:40:35.780
Thanks, Josh.
谢谢你，乔希。

00:40:36.929 --> 00:40:37.982
That's so cool.
太酷了。

00:40:37.982 --> 00:40:42.050
Did you have any idea that the Spanish translation was so?
你以前知道西班牙语翻译这么厉害吗？

00:40:42.050 --> 00:40:43.904
No, but I love that getting a shout out.
不知道，但我很高兴能得到这样的赞赏。

00:40:43.904 --> 00:40:46.130
That's quite worthy of a shout out and I didn't.
这绝对值得称赞，而我之前并不知道。

00:40:46.130 --> 00:40:47.313
I don't know that I've ever heard that.
我不知道我是否曾听说过这一点。

00:40:47.313 --> 00:40:47.889
That's really cool.
这真的很酷。

00:40:47.889 --> 00:40:49.489
The silent heroes, the trans members.
无名英雄，翻译工作者们。

00:40:49.489 --> 00:40:51.659
It is, and the show is so international.
确实，而且这部剧太国际化了。

00:40:51.659 --> 00:40:54.860
It does go places really well, and maybe that's part of it.
它在各地都很受欢迎，也许这就是原因之一。

00:40:54.860 --> 00:40:57.409
There was really good dubbing done for Spanish.
西班牙语的配音做得非常好。

00:40:57.409 --> 00:40:58.079
That's great.
太棒了。

00:40:58.079 --> 00:41:01.889
I love hearing that, and I love hearing from a member of our armed forces.
听到这些我很高兴，听到来自我们武装部队成员的声音我也很高兴。

00:41:01.889 --> 00:41:07.937
We hear over and over again from people who are on deployments, that this show was some kind of comfort.
我们一次又一次地听到那些在海外执行任务的人说，这部剧提供了一种慰藉。

00:41:07.937 --> 00:41:12.821
Even though this wasn't exactly the story here, this was more like when he got back.
尽管这不完全是这里的叙事，这更像是他回来之后的事。

00:41:12.821 --> 00:41:14.449
It's very cool to hear that.
听到这些真的很酷。

00:41:14.449 --> 00:41:39.289
I also feel a special kind of warmth when I hear people deployed overseas or even in battle zones, living potentially dangerous moments and having this as a way to escape or past the time.
当我听说身处海外甚至战区、经历着潜在危险时刻的人们，将此作为一种逃避或打发时间的方式时，我也有一种特别的温暖感。

00:41:39.289 --> 00:41:40.289
I find it very moving.
我觉得这非常感人。

00:41:40.289 --> 00:42:07.957
I don't remember what season this was, Craig, but I got a letter from a soldier who was stationed overseas that he it was so Wonderful this letter and he it was almost the same story his for his buddies had started watching it They were doing all the inside jokes, and he felt kind of left out But he was also like I don't want to watch this stupid show and then he one of his buddies just gave him the first season DVD and he watched it and he flipped for it And he also told me he was depressed.
克雷格，我不记得这是第几季了，但我收到了一位驻扎在海外的士兵的信，他的信太美妙了，几乎是同样的故事：他的四个朋友开始看这部剧，他们在玩各种只有内部才懂的梗，他觉得自己有点被冷落了，但他的态度是“我才不想看这部愚蠢的节目”，后来他的一个朋友把第一季的DVD给了他，他看了之后就彻底迷上了。他还告诉我他当时患有抑郁症。

00:42:07.957 --> 00:42:40.969
He was he had fallen into like a depression Yeah, and he said the only way you could tell what the days were where he was either in Iraq or Afghanistan was like in the in the mess hall was like that each day had a different food and that was like the only way he could tell it was like Wednesday or Thursday but he wrote me this letter and he said he called his wife and he said this show is making me really happy it's like the only thing that's making me happy so awesome can you start watching it and I'm gonna tell you where to stop so when I get home we can like just pick it up together.
他陷入了抑郁之中，是的，他说在伊拉克或阿富汗，他唯一能知道今天是星期几的方法就是在食堂里，每天都有不同的食物，那是他唯一能分清是星期三还是星期四的方式，但他写了这封信给我，他说他给妻子打电话，说这部剧让他真的很高兴，这是唯一让他高兴的事，所以太棒了，你能开始看吗？我会告诉你该在哪个地方停下来，这样等我回家后，我们就可以一起接着看了。

00:42:40.969 --> 00:42:41.809
It's a great sign like that.
这真的是个很好的迹象。

00:42:41.809 --> 00:42:45.010
And I was so moved by it that I wrote him back.
我深受感动，于是给他回了信。

00:42:45.010 --> 00:42:50.130
And then when he was back home, him and his wife came to set.
后来他回国后，他和他的妻子来到了片场。

00:42:50.130 --> 00:42:51.449
We brought them to set.
我们把他们带到了片场。

00:42:51.449 --> 00:42:52.289
That's right.
没错。

00:42:52.289 --> 00:42:53.130
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

00:42:53.130 --> 00:42:54.610
Right now I do, that's amazing.
现在我想起来了，这太惊人了。

00:42:54.610 --> 00:42:56.130
And I stay in touch with him for a little while.
我和他保持了一段时间的联系。

00:42:56.130 --> 00:42:59.769
I don't know where he is, but he- Hopefully he's hearing this.
我不知道他在哪里，但他——希望他能听到这个。

00:42:59.769 --> 00:43:00.769
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:43:00.769 --> 00:43:02.289
But it was really sweet.
但那真的很暖心。

00:43:02.289 --> 00:43:21.650
And there's something about, again, we talk a lot about people in, going through tough life transitions, but also like being overseas like in the armed forces and whether you're in like a really dangerous zone or a zone where kind of nothing's happening and you're away from your family.
而且关于这一点，我们经常谈论那些经历艰难人生转折的人，还有身处海外武装部队的人，无论你是在极其危险的地区，还是在一个似乎什么都没发生、远离家人的地区。

00:43:21.650 --> 00:43:32.010
Like there's a lot that one might need some sense of comfort or familiarity or some sense of back-homeness.
人们可能会非常需要一种安慰感、熟悉感，或者某种回家的感觉。

00:43:32.010 --> 00:43:37.489
We've heard this so many times about people and deployments around the world that this was the connection to home.
我们听过太多次关于世界各地执行任务的人们的故事，这部剧就是他们与家的联系。

00:43:37.489 --> 00:43:44.969
How much of it was a connection to home and that people would watch it together in barracks and like, and I don't know, that really warms my heart.
它在多大程度上成为了与家的联系，人们在兵营里一起观看，而且……我不知道，这真的温暖了我的心。

00:43:44.969 --> 00:43:45.809
I really love that.
我真的很喜欢这一点。

00:43:45.809 --> 00:43:48.769
So thank you to everybody who has served our country.
所以感谢所有为我们国家服役的人。

00:43:48.769 --> 00:43:49.650
Yeah, thanks Josh.
是的，谢谢你，乔希。

00:43:49.650 --> 00:43:57.610
Thanks for that letter and shout out to all the people overseas who are on military bases who are watching the show.
感谢那封信，并向所有在海外军事基地观看本剧的人们致敬。

00:43:57.610 --> 00:44:01.489
And if you're loving this podcast, please spread the word.
如果你喜欢这个播客，请帮忙宣传。

00:44:01.489 --> 00:44:06.130
We're so happy to spend this time with you and we'll see you next time.
我们很高兴能与大家共度这段时光，我们下期再见。

